      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Omeprazole reduces acid, but it doesn't entirely block the direct inflammation-causing effects of ibuprofen on the stomach lining. Since you are insisting on taking Advil, take it with a full glass of water and consider eating a small amount of food beforehand to provide some buffer. However, for reliable relief and safety, it is best to have a doctor assess why your stomach ache remains despite the Omeprazole.",
      "source": "target",
